1
00:00:00,105 --> 00:00:04,265
The Inspiration mock puts the image collection beside a boards sidebar,

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:06,173
with tag filters above it.

3
00:00:06,474 --> 00:00:09,778
Card overlays show titles and photographer labels.

4
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:13,554
These names and images are demonstration placeholders.

5
00:00:15,172 --> 00:00:19,450
Here is the real Angular interface with the same first twelve images.

6
00:00:19,764 --> 00:00:23,566
The heading, navigation, restrained colours, and image grid carry

7
00:00:23,566 --> 00:00:24,121
through.

8
00:00:24,435 --> 00:00:28,645
This recording uses in-memory fixtures, with no production writes

9
00:00:28,645 --> 00:00:30,147
or AI requests.

10
00:00:31,745 --> 00:00:34,234
The difference is visible side by side.

11
00:00:34,548 --> 00:00:37,484
The mock has boards, counts, and tag filters.

12
00:00:37,811 --> 00:00:42,087
The current page uses the full width for references, with saved status

13
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:44,089
and dates in the card captions.

14
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:48,352
Boards, filtering, and on-card board actions are still mock-only.

15
00:00:49,945 --> 00:00:52,947
The collection opens with twenty-four references.

16
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,565
Load more brings in the remaining item.

17
00:00:55,866 --> 00:00:59,985
Titles open each saved reference, keeping browsing separate from the

18
00:00:59,985 --> 00:01:03,368
detailed source information and personal study notes.

19
00:01:04,972 --> 00:01:07,947
A reference opens into its own detail page.

20
00:01:08,275 --> 00:01:12,658
The photograph stays connected to its source, attribution, and notes.

21
00:01:12,959 --> 00:01:17,288
Edit metadata lets us record what to study, then save that context

22
00:01:17,288 --> 00:01:19,092
back to the fixture library.

23
00:01:20,692 --> 00:01:24,982
Save link keeps a source URL with an optional title, attribution,

24
00:01:24,982 --> 00:01:25,812
and notes.

25
00:01:26,113 --> 00:01:28,549
Saving opens a link-only reference.

26
00:01:28,863 --> 00:01:31,773
It does not invent a preview or fetch the source.

27
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,904
The separate import action is shown here but is not submitted.

28
00:01:37,505 --> 00:01:40,612
This is a deliberately simulated loading failure.

29
00:01:40,926 --> 00:01:43,915
The page gives a clear error and a retry action.

30
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,704
Retrying restores the image collection.

31
00:01:47,018 --> 00:01:50,939
The demonstration verifies the recovery as well as the successful

32
00:01:50,939 --> 00:01:52,099
browsing path.

33
00:01:53,705 --> 00:01:58,021
At three hundred and seventy-five pixels, the working collection reflows

34
00:01:58,021 --> 00:02:00,891
to fit the screen without horizontal scrolling.

35
00:02:01,205 --> 00:02:05,416
The save and upload entry points remain available, and each reference

36
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:07,207
still opens through its title.

37
00:02:08,798 --> 00:02:12,932
The working page delivers collection browsing, reference details,

38
00:02:13,009 --> 00:02:15,182
notes, and saving source links.

39
00:02:15,483 --> 00:02:18,484
The mock goes further with boards and tag filtering.

40
00:02:18,798 --> 00:02:23,364
This comparison preserves those visible gaps, so the video demonstrates

41
00:02:23,364 --> 00:02:25,063
the current product honestly.
